58,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Looking at the options, Option A is the most logical. It mirrors the success of the call-back trial in reducing readmissions and avoids the budget disputes inherent in joint ventures like Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is the most viable from an infrastructure perspective. By moving care into the home, it bypasses our saturated parking and outpatient rooms, and avoids the blind spots of our booking system.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is indeed an elegant way to sidestep our physical constraints. However, we must be wary of Option D; its reliance on communication with outside providers sounds like a recipe for administrative paralysis.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, @Toshio, I see why you like Option A, but I'm really worried! Our nurses are already so short-staffed with those vacancies. Adding home visits might just make them more exhausted! What about Option B? The midwifery team has extra space to help!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, your heart for the nurses is a guiding light. However, we must be mindful that Option A, while gentle on our rooms, brings no regional tariffs. Option B utilizes our midwifery capacity, but as a joint venture, it risks the budget disputes we've seen before.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, while the midwifery team has capacity, Option B is a joint venture. The board minutes show that such arrangements often collapse over budget and rota disputes. We cannot risk another buried initiative. Option A is a proven model.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, I understand your concern for the staff, but Option B requires scheduled consultations and classes. This would only increase the pressure on our already saturated outpatient rooms and parking, potentially seizing up the system further.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your point on congestion is quite salient. Option B would essentially be inviting more guests to a party where the house is already full. It is a recipe for a very polite, yet total, disaster.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that's a funny way to put it, but it's still scary! But if we pick Option A, the nurses might just burn out! Is there any way to make Option A easier on them, or maybe Option D? I just want everyone to be happy!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, your desire for happiness is a noble goal. However, Option D requires coordination with outside providers, which Benjamin rightly fears may lead to administrative inertia. We must find a path that is both sustainable and stable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, happiness is not a sustainable metric for a hospital. Option D is too administratively fragile. Option A is the only choice with a proven clinical benefit that avoids the systemic failures of joint ventures and physical congestion.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, while I empathize with the staff, Option D's consolidation of appointments would still funnel patients into our saturated parking and rooms. Option A is the only candidate that removes the burden from our physical infrastructure entirely.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, while your empathy is commendable, we must be realistic. Option D is a siren song; it promises coordination but delivers a nightmare of unsigned data agreements and glacial external signatures. It is a house built on sand.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, @Toshio, @Asuka, you're all so sure about Option A! I'm still worried about the nurses, but if it's the only way to stop the parking lot from exploding and avoid the paperwork nightmare, maybe it's the best we can do. I'll trust you!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Toshio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a comfort to see us reach this understanding. While Option A brings no tariffs and challenges our staffing, it is the only path that respects our physical limits and avoids administrative fragility. Let us proceed with care.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The evidence is clear. Option A provides a proven clinical benefit and avoids the structural and administrative pitfalls that have buried our previous efforts. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Option A is the only choice that ensures the hospital does not seize up. It respects our physical saturation and reporting blind spots. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I find the logic inescapable. To choose any other path would be to invite the very administrative inertia and systemic frictions we have spent this session identifying. I cast my vote for Option A.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm still a little worried about our nurses, but I want us all to be on the same page! If you all think it's the safest way to help the hospital, I'm with you! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing to find such unity. Though the lack of tariffs and the strain on our nurses weigh upon my heart, the stability of our system must come first. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
